-- Section 202(b) and (c): the extended compensation account, and interstate claims.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Section 202(b)(1) says the State law shall establish an account "not less than" the least of
-- three amounts. These rules compute that least amount: the floor the State law must meet.
-- A State law may give more (the Act sets a floor, not a ceiling); the amount below is what the
-- Act requires and what section 204(b) counts as sharable.
-- The relation: the individual holds a claim, up to the account, against the State, which bears the
-- duty to pay; the State's own law decides how it divides the account into weekly payments.
-- out of text: the State law's weekly benefit amount, its regular compensation, its decision
-- to reduce the account by additional compensation, and the unemployment statistics that decide
-- whether a high unemployment period is in effect: plain inputs.

§ `Section 202(b): the individual's compensation account`

§§ `202(b)(2): the weekly benefit amount`

-- src:61 | “(2) For purposes of paragraph (1), an individual’s weekly benefit amount for a week is the amount of regular compensation (including dependents’ allowances) under the State law payable to such individual for such week for total unemployment.
@ref s 202(b)(2) (src:61)
GIVEN `regular compensation payable for the week for total unemployment` IS A NUMBER
      `dependents' allowances payable for the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly benefit amount for a week` `regular compensation payable for the week for total unemployment` `dependents' allowances payable for the week` MEANS
    `regular compensation payable for the week for total unemployment` PLUS `dependents' allowances payable for the week`

§§ `202(b)(3): the high unemployment period`

-- src:67 | the term ‘high unemployment period’ means any period during which an extended benefit period would be in effect if section 203(f)(1)(A)(i) were applied by substituting ‘8 percent’ for ‘6.5 percent’.
@ref s 202(b)(3)(B) (src:67)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage substituted in section 202(b)(3)(B)` MEANS 8

-- One weekly reading for the high unemployment period: the week is "on" if the alternative
-- trigger test is met at 8 per cent, whether or not the State law has adopted that trigger.
-- src:67 | “(B) For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term ‘high unemployment period’ means any period during which an extended benefit period would be in effect if section 203(f)(1)(A)(i) were applied by substituting ‘8 percent’ for ‘6.5 percent’.
@ref s 202(b)(3)(B) (src:67)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Total unemployment reading`
GIVETH AN `Indicator reading`
`the reading for the high unemployment period` week reading MEANS
    `Indicator reading` WITH
        `week beginning` IS week
        `State on indicator` IS `the alternative trigger test is met at the percentage` week reading `the percentage substituted in section 202(b)(3)(B)`

-- The period is the extended benefit period that those readings would give (euca-s203-period).
-- NOTHING means that no extended benefit period would be in effect.
-- src:67 | “(B) For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term ‘high unemployment period’ means any period during which an extended benefit period would be in effect if section 203(f)(1)(A)(i) were applied by substituting ‘8 percent’ for ‘6.5 percent’.
@ref s 202(b)(3)(B) (src:67)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `the extended benefit period that would be in effect` IS A MAYBE `Extended benefit period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the week begins in a high unemployment period` week `the extended benefit period that would be in effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the extended benefit period that would be in effect`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST period THEN `the week begins in the extended benefit period` week period

§§ `202(b)(1) and (3)(A): the amount the account must hold`

-- Under (3)(A), in a high unemployment period the figures become 80 per centum, twenty and
-- forty-six in place of 50 per centum, thirteen and thirty-nine.
-- src:57 | “(A) 50 per centum of the total amount of regular compensation (including dependents’ allowances) payable to him during such benefit year under such law,
-- src:63 | (A) Effective with respect to weeks beginning in a high unemployment period, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting—
-- src:64 | “(i) ‘80 per centum’ for ‘50 per centum’ in subparagraph (A),
-- src:65 | “(ii) ‘twenty’ for ‘thirteen’ in subparagraph (B), and
-- src:66 | “(iii) ‘forty-six’ for ‘thirty-nine’ in subparagraph (C).
@ref s 202(b)(1)(A) and (3)(A)(i) (src:57 src:63-66)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(A)` account MEANS
    (IF account's `the week begins in a high unemployment period` THEN 0.8 ELSE 0.5)
        TIMES account's `total regular compensation payable during the benefit year, including dependents' allowances`

-- src:58 | “(B) thirteen times his average weekly benefit amount, or
-- src:63 | (A) Effective with respect to weeks beginning in a high unemployment period, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting—
-- src:64 | “(i) ‘80 per centum’ for ‘50 per centum’ in subparagraph (A),
-- src:65 | “(ii) ‘twenty’ for ‘thirteen’ in subparagraph (B), and
-- src:66 | “(iii) ‘forty-six’ for ‘thirty-nine’ in subparagraph (C).
@ref s 202(b)(1)(B) and (3)(A)(ii) (src:58 src:63-66)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(B)` account MEANS
    (IF account's `the week begins in a high unemployment period` THEN 20 ELSE 13)
        TIMES account's `average weekly benefit amount`

-- src:59 | “(C) thirty-nine times his average weekly benefit amount, reduced by the regular compensation paid (or deemed paid) to him during such benefit year under such law;
-- src:63 | (A) Effective with respect to weeks beginning in a high unemployment period, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting—
-- src:64 | “(i) ‘80 per centum’ for ‘50 per centum’ in subparagraph (A),
-- src:65 | “(ii) ‘twenty’ for ‘thirteen’ in subparagraph (B), and
-- src:66 | “(iii) ‘forty-six’ for ‘thirty-nine’ in subparagraph (C).
@ref s 202(b)(1)(C) and (3)(A)(iii) (src:59 src:63-66)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(C)` account MEANS
    ((IF account's `the week begins in a high unemployment period` THEN 46 ELSE 39) TIMES account's `average weekly benefit amount`)
        MINUS account's `regular compensation paid or deemed paid during the benefit year`

-- src:56 | The amount established in such account shall be not less than whichever of the following is the least:
@ref s 202(b)(1) (src:56)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` account MEANS
    `the smallest of three amounts`
        (`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(A)` account)
        (`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(B)` account)
        (`the amount under section 202(b)(1)(C)` account)

-- src:60 | except that the amount so determined shall (if the State law so provides) be reduced by the aggregate amount of additional compensation paid (or deemed paid) to him under such law for prior weeks of unemployment in such benefit year which did not begin in an extended benefit period.
@ref s 202(b)(1), closing words (src:60)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the extended compensation account must hold` account MEANS
    `the least of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` account
        MINUS (IF account's `the State law reduces the account by additional compensation paid`
               THEN account's `additional compensation paid or deemed paid for prior weeks in the benefit year that did not begin in an extended benefit period`
               ELSE 0)

-- How many whole weeks the account pays for, if the weekly amount of extended compensation is
-- the weekly benefit amount. That the weekly amount of extended compensation is the State law's
-- weekly benefit amount is s 202(a)(2) (the State law's terms for regular compensation apply);
-- the figure itself is out of text.
-- src:56 | “(b) [Individual’s Compensation Accounts] (1) The State law shall provide that the State will establish, for each eligible individual who files an application therefor, an extended compensation account with respect to such individual’s benefit year. The amount established in such account shall be not less than whichever of the following is the least:
-- src:61 | “(2) For purposes of paragraph (1), an individual’s weekly benefit amount for a week is the amount of regular compensation (including dependents’ allowances) under the State law payable to such individual for such week for total unemployment.
@ref s 202(b)(1) and (2) (src:56 src:61)
GIVEN account IS AN `Account facts`
      `the weekly amount of extended compensation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of whole weeks the extended compensation account covers` account `the weekly amount of extended compensation` MEANS
    IF `the weekly amount of extended compensation` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the greater of two amounts` 0 (FLOOR (`the amount the extended compensation account must hold` account DIVIDED BY `the weekly amount of extended compensation`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 202(c): interstate claims in a State with no extended benefit period`

§§ `202(c)(2): the first two weeks`

-- src:71 | “(2) Paragraph (1) shall not apply with respect to the first 2 weeks for which extended compensation is payable (determined without regard to this subsection) pursuant to an interstate claim filed under the interstate benefit payment plan to the individual from the extended compensation account established for the benefit year.
@ref s 202(c)(2) (src:71)
GIVEN claim IS AN `Interstate claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the week is one of the first 2 weeks payable pursuant to the interstate claim` claim MEANS
    claim's `earlier weeks for which extended compensation was payable pursuant to the interstate claim from the account` LESS THAN 2

§§ `202(c)(1): payment stops`

-- src:68 | “(c) [Cessation of Extended Benefits When Paid Under an Interstate Claim in a State Where Extended Benefit Period Is Not in Effect] (1) Except as provided in paragraph (2), payment of extended compensation shall not be made to any individual for any week if—
-- src:69 | “(A) extended compensation would (but for this subsection) have been payable for such week pursuant to an interstate claim filed in any State under the interstate benefit payment plan, and
-- src:70 | “(B) an extended benefit period is not in effect for such week in such State.
@ref s 202(c)(1) (src:68-70)
GIVEN claim IS AN `Interstate claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`payment of extended compensation is not made for the week under section 202(c)(1)` claim MEANS
        claim's `extended compensation would but for the cessation rule have been payable for the week pursuant to an interstate claim under the interstate benefit payment plan`
    AND (NOT claim's `an extended benefit period is in effect for the week in the State where the claim was filed`)
    AND (NOT `the week is one of the first 2 weeks payable pursuant to the interstate claim` claim)

§§ `202(c)(3): section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code`

-- out of text: section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code. The text says only that it "shall
-- not apply to any denial of compensation required under this subsection".
-- src:72 | “(3) Section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 shall not apply to any denial of compensation required under this subsection.
@ref s 202(c)(3) (src:72)
GIVEN `compensation is denied as section 202(c)(1) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3304(a)(9)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code does not apply to the denial` `compensation is denied as section 202(c)(1) requires` MEANS
    `compensation is denied as section 202(c)(1) requires`
